## CODING STANDARDS

- TypeScript strict mode ON. Never use `any` — use `unknown` and narrow it.
- Always define return types on non-trivial functions.
- `async/await` over `.then()`. `const` by default, `let` only when needed. Never `var`.
- All API route handlers return typed `NextResponse` objects.
- Consistent error shape: `{ "error": { "code": "ERROR_CODE", "message": "..." } }`
- Consistent success shape: `{ "data": ... }`
- All API routes versioned under `/api/v1/`.
- `firebase-admin` never imported in client components — use `server-only` guard.
- Always null-check or optional-chain potentially undefined Firestore fields.
- No `useEffect` for data fetching — use React Server Components or SWR/fetch in hooks.
- Keep components under ~150 lines. Split if larger.
- Add JSDoc comments to all API route handlers.

