## FIRESTORE DATA MODEL

```
users/{userId}
users/{userId}/plans/{planId}
users/{userId}/plans/{planId}/semesters/{semesterId}
users/{userId}/events/{eventId}
courses/{courseId}    ← shared, read-only, populated by scraper only
```

- Always use Firestore `serverTimestamp()` — never `new Date()`.
- `courses` collection is read-only at runtime.
- Never expose raw Firestore document IDs in API responses without intention.

